{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Arm yourselves from among you.</b> Gird your warriors — even though he heard that his death depended on this matter, he did not delay. And they said in the Midrash: Joshua did not do so. When he came to wage war against the thirty-one kings, he said: If I slay them, I shall die immediately, just as happened to Moses immediately when he defeated the kings of Midian. What did he do? He began with one and drew out his waging of war, as it is said (Joshua 11): ״ימים רבים עשה יהושע את כל המלכים האלה מלחמה״. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: So you have done — I shall shorten your years by ten years, for he was worthy to live 110 years like Moses our master, peace be upon him, but he lived only 100 years. This is what is written (Proverbs 19): ״רבות מחשבות בלב איש ועצת ה' היא תקום״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The prooftext cites Joshua 11 but the verse reference in the canonical text is Joshua 11:18; the citation appears abbreviated. The Midrashic chronology taken at face value: Joshua lived 110 years per Joshua 24:29, not 100; the text reads ק״י (110) where logic expects ק״ (100), rendered exactly as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:13.114847098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}